# Unified-diff fixtures represent a blank context line as a single space, so a
# whitespace check would flag every one of them. Stripping it would corrupt the diff,
# which the pair harness reconstructs and compares byte-for-byte at prepare time.
Evals/Behavioral-Harness/experiments/**/fixtures/**/*.diff -whitespace

# These artifacts are pinned by byte digest. A Windows checkout must preserve the
# reviewed LF bytes rather than turning an intact fixture into an integrity failure.
Evals/Verification-Surface/** text eol=lf
tools/b2_*.py text eol=lf
